ything ready and then elena comes up  with the idea of launching the supplies  towards venus to use that to slingshot  it back towards mars it will take longer  than doing it in the window but it'll  still beat danielle and her crew there  by a few months unsurprisingly the  soviets announced that they'll follow  suit and now we know why we saw at the  end of season 2 that there were people  on mars in 1995. in her debate with bill  clinton on the campaign trail you see  ellen score some points by being for the  accelerated timeline this is something  americans can get behind  seeing her in this different arena away  from her astronaut life underlines how  much everything is going to change in  the future of this series it was great  to see that nasa ingenuity and everyone  working together to solve these problems  one more time but by the end of this  episode you have to wonder who will even  be there after the dust settles elada is  poised to take over if margot goes down  but who is left to take over for dany as  she ages out in orbit you see that the  polaris hotel looks a lot different now  those methane engines have been added  and it's becoming the phoenix deb is  taking ed and karen on a tour he  mentioned some of the upgrades and some  mobile hab modules and that they have  added triple redundancies to make sure  the thrusters don't malfunction again  there's a moment where karen stops as  she walks past the elevator where sam  died that reminds us of what happened  the last time they used this ship and  when they get to the flight deck the  inevitable happens dev starts laying out  his vision for things he wants to  automate most of the flight controls and  load up the crew with scientists and  even a poet and it almost feels like a  setup because obviously if you're  bringing on this dinosaur test pilot  he's never gonna go for any of that and  of course ed objects dev then makes a  big scene of stopping the work and  apologizing for making this huge mistake  telling the crew that they need to  rework the flight control systems per  the commander of the ship immediately  and i don't know it works it makes ed  feel like he's got control but the way  it played out and the spectacle of it  feels a little fishy to me  kelly comes in to ask danielle if she'll  keep her on nasa's mission she makes her  case it's more science focused as she is  and even though she's been offered a  slot on helios's trip she wants to go on  the mission where she's not just there  because her dad is the commander she's  been searching for life in the most  inhospitable place on earth and they'll  need her expertise when they get to mars  danny seems impressed and ultimately  agrees to put her on the mission so i  guess that's at least part of the answer  about who might be at nasa in the future  later in the training sim the other  danny seems distracted and crashes which  danny finds a lot less impressive he  tells her he's got a lot going on that  he just closed on a house and so she  lets him go home and basically tells him  to go romance his wife as he leaves the  building he sees the statue of his  parents outside which is a nice touch  and then later he goes to the bar to get  drunk there's a woman there who's  flirting with him pretty heavily and he  sees karen come in so he asks her if she  wants to leave they go to the swimming  pool at his old house and the new owners  call the cops they do let him go because  he's an astronaut and they know his  famous father but they call jsc and  danny has to come to pick him up in  their conversation there's a mention of  a car crash that happened eight years  ago and he tries to play off the fact  that he's drinking again she wants him  to provoke his flight status and go get  help and tells him he needs to get  himself straight and that he should go  to his wife for help karen had come into  the outpost to try to poach aleda away  from nasa she makes her a generous offer  and goes the route of saying that if she  stays there she'll always be in margot's  shadow elena decides to stay loyal and  to make her point she shows her the moon  rock she brought back and tells her that  margot made that possible she tells her  if she has to be called margo's girl  that's a small price to pay the next  morning we catch up with her at home  with her husband who isn't thrilled she  turned on the offer it is a lot more  money they argue and she makes the case  that they're doing fine compared to  where she came from and we do hear more  that indicates that her father is  starting to show signs of dementia she  says that she hasn't seen any of that  and it's really that she's not trying to  see it and her husband points out yeah  maybe that's because she's never there  we see amber stevens at home and danny  comes in planning to tell her something  probably about his relapse and not going  to mars but before he can get into any  of it ed gives him a call and offers him  a spot on helios mission his ass is  saved and i'm not sure if that knows  what he's getting himself into by  bringing on someone who's obsessed with  his ex-wife as his wingman danny does  come into helios to try to change his  mind but he thinks this is all just  because dany needs a purpose the same  way that gordo needed a purpose when he  sent him back to the moon and with a guy  like ed that's just that no one's really  gonna change his mind he comes in to  tell his team and make the announcement  and that's when we see karen get shaken  up later at the outpost kelly breaks the  news that she'll be going with nasa and  that she was the one who asked danielle  to put her on that mission at first ed  looks hurt but he ends up being  supportive so i skipped over the cold  open because it all sets up what happens  next in that we have flashbacks to iac  conferences in london over the years  this is where margot and sergey see each  other and in the first one we see them  enter an elevator together after finally  having that drink that they talked about  at the end of season two there's clear  romantic tension that's left over from  his trip to the states but she rushes  out the door as soon as it arrives on  her floor as he stands there staring at  her longingly and i do think it's worth  mentioning that there's a very  deliberate shot to get you to notice  that he's wearing a wedding ring in this  first sequence over the years we see  that they continue to see each other  here and basically the same things  happen and it's all to play up this idea  of will they or won't they at different  points we see one of the others stop  when they get out of the elevator  or hold the door and in 1991 he finally  makes his move and touches her hand and  in this shot you can see that he's no  longer wearing that wedding ring the  setup here was great because she puts  her hand in a place where it looks like  she's inviting him to hold it but it's  all very subtle it fits with her  character there's the relief that it  finally happens and then disappointment  when the elevator stops and this other  guy gets in and they have to pretend  like nothing's going on sergey pauses  when it's time to leave hoping that  she'll follow him but because this guy  knows who they are she just says good  night and sends him away  fast forward to the present day they're  back in london and this time deb is  there laying on the charm margo and  sergey meet up again and they watch him  and discuss how his entering the space  race is changing things they have drinks  and then later while they're standing at  the bar the bartender tells them that  it's last call margot says she can use  another drink and tell sergey to grab  the bottle and it's on they don't say  anything in the elevator he uses the  bathroom and while he's in there she  looks in the mirror and it reminds you  that this moment was 10 years in the  making and we see him do the same thing  and it appears that there's this shared  reservation but we know there's more  going on with what he's thinking about  he comes out and when he starts to make  small talk and pour the drink she  interrupts saying i would like you to  kiss me it all starts out pretty awkward  it's pretty obvious that this is not  margo's comfort zone but it does start  to get hot and then sergey stops in a  monumentally unromantic move he starts  talking about work he explains that they  can't get their nuclear engine cooling  system to work and begs her and i mean  begs her to help because if he fails  there will be serious consequences she  points out that they have this agreement  they trade secrets to help each other  out as far as space is concerned but  anything that could be used for military  use is off the table he tries to bring  her around but eventually he gives up  saying he understands and that he  apologizes for everything which seems a  little out of place as soon as he says  that there's a knock at the door and  then you understand what he was saying  and before they open it there's a great  shot of her where you see that she  starts to realize what she's gotten  herself into intelligence agents come in  they show her compromising photos  they've collected showing her talking  with sergey she's still adamant about  not sharing the engine design but the  agents point out that she's been sharing  classified information with them for  nine years her comeback is that anything  she shared was for the furtherance of  space travel and in the interest of  international peace which of course is  naive and the agent points out that the  fbi would consider her a spy and a  traitor still she's willing to take that  chance and when they see that she's  serious they start strangling sergey  right in front of her the threat is  explicit if she doesn't help they'll  kill him and they give her a day to  think about it and a telephone number to  call when she's ready when she comes  back in the office we see that there's a  tear in her eye nori mentions the  delivery from neptune records which is  the way that her and sergey stayed in  touch and she tells them to send it back  in her office bill is waiting and he's  there to tell her that he's going to  helios i guess they went after him after  elena turned them down he says it's not  personal and you believe it he was  totally dedicated to nasa it's just a  whole lot of money and he explains it a  little better to elena later she doesn't  say anything to him on his way out then  after he's gone she says goodbye bill to  herself and picks up the photo of when  she was just starting that he was  looking at she puts the number the agent  gave her on her desk where we can see it  elena and bill do have their goodbyes he  almost tears up when he says that she'll  be a great flight director and she calls  him peanut to lighten the mood he says  that her and margot are like two peas in  a pod and given what we just saw with  her situation it does hint that elate is  going to be very important at nasa  there's a shot where we see her working  late at night which is something that we  know that she always does and when it  transitions to the next scene it's two  years later and it's launch day and you  guessed it she is the flight director  for the mars mission and i have to give  coral pena credit here she does these  scenes so well it really gets you pumped  up to see her in that position and it is  still a race to get there first we see  ed and danny launch from orbit on  phoenix  sojourner one lift off from the moon  it's our first shot of what the  sojourner craft looks like and then we  see the soviet mars 94 mission take off  as margot looks on considering this is  two years later that their ship is  taking off it's heavily implied that she  did give them the secrets that they  needed and you understand the  uncomfortable look on her face nori  comes in to tell her the president is on  the line and it is ellen she won a race  and now nasa is trying to win theirs and  the episode ends there  so this episode was just for all mankind  doing what it does best across the board  even when it does things it's done  before like the last minute time jump to  kick things up for the next episode it  still works like a charm there were a  lot of nice references to make us feel  at home bill raising his hand in the  meeting elena being comfortable with her  scarring alone with her husband in their  room and ed dumping all the cheese on a  spaghetti that all makes the time we've  spent getting to know these characters  feel worth it the ending also manages to  be hopeful while there's all that  impending catastrophe right under the  surface as a big fan of margot and the  ways they've made her a complicated  character that part of things was  particularly tough but i do like that  bending the rules for something that  seems like it's for the greater good is  much easier for her to navigate  emotionally than being intimate with  someone she clearly cares about in  sergey obviously what the kgb agent told  her was correct good intentions aside  she really did walk right into it and  because she's given her life to the job  in the space program the weak spots that  will be her downfall are completely  believable i guess the one silver lining  is that her close colleague now happens  to have a job that comes with get out of  jail free cards but losing the work  that's gonna crush her in her later  years as much as i am hoping to see ed  knock danny stevens down a peg i'm still  sentimentally rooting for nasa in this  race the crane shot after the time jump  at mission control where you watch  eleida come out from behind the flight  desk pretty much says it all they may  now be the past and ed not being able to  get there first again would be somewhat  disappointing but nothing else about  helios has brought me on board yet the  jury is still out on deb iesa but  especially on my second watch the way he  did that quick turn with ed it just came  off as suspicious rather than anything  else you do have to hand it to them  though ed danny and their crew are  traveling in style compared to everyone  else i like that they didn't mess around  too much with the presidential race  since it seemed like an inevitability  that ellen would win but that also meant  that we didn't get to spend much time  with the character which is kind of a  shame the reveal was pretty fantastic  though and i'm sure we'll get more of  her as this race heats up as a layman  the sojourner one wasn't very exciting  when we finally saw it to me it just  looked like a bigger version of the  shuttles that they use with some  modifications it's very possible that  i'm missing something and it's weird  that we haven't been introduced to four  out of the six people that are on it i  was a little surprised that we didn't  see molly in helios mission control i do  wonder what she's been up to for the  last two years and i think that is a  good place to leave things let me know  in the comments what you thought about  the episode and how you think things are  gonna play out there are a lot of  different possibilities and a lot of  potential so let me know what you think  please like this video if you enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already and thanks for watching  i'll talk to you soon

